cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use TensorGuard or its frozen real-world bug benchmark corpus, please
  cite this repository.
title: "TensorGuard: sound static shape/device/dtype/phase/gradient verification for PyTorch"
abstract: >-
  TensorGuard is a sound, static verifier for PyTorch nn.Module architectures.
  It proves the absence of (or finds) shape, device, dtype, training-phase, and
  gradient bugs using refinement types discharged by an SMT solver together with
  a reduced-product abstract domain, with no model execution, no concrete
  inputs, and no GPU. The repository also ships a frozen, content-addressed,
  labeled real-world bug benchmark corpus (real_benchmarks/) as a standalone,
  citable contribution.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The TensorGuard maintainers"
    website: "https://github.com/thehalleyyoung/tensorguard"
repository-code: "https://github.com/thehalleyyoung/tensorguard"
url: "https://github.com/thehalleyyoung/tensorguard"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
keywords:
  - PyTorch
  - static analysis
  - refinement types
  - abstract interpretation
  - SMT
  - shape checking
  - machine learning reliability
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "TensorGuard real-world PyTorch bug benchmark corpus"
    abstract: >-
      A frozen, versioned, content-addressed (SHA-256) corpus of real PyTorch
      nn.Module architectures, each labeled clean (should verify SAFE) or buggy
      (should verify UNSAFE), spanning the shape, device, training-phase, and
      gradient domains. See real_benchmarks/DATASHEET.md.
    authors:
      - name: "The TensorGuard maintainers"
    version: "1.0.0"
    license: MIT
    repository-code: "https://github.com/thehalleyyoung/tensorguard"
